{
  "dom_id": "step-q178619",
  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "Expressed as a fraction in its simplest form, $\\frac{5}{8}÷(-\\frac{3}{4})=${{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "Dividing a positive number by a negative number gives a negative number. Hence, the result will be negative.\n\nTherefore, since\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{8}÷\\frac{3}{4}=\\frac{5\\times 4}{8\\times 3}=\\frac{20}{24}=\\frac{5}{6},\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{6}÷(-\\frac{3}{4})=-\\frac{5}{6}.\n$$",
